#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
===============================================================================
 SMI Analyzer  -  MICROSAR Safe (Vector Safety Manual) SMI verification tool
===============================================================================

Statically analyses a MICROSAR sandbox (application sources, generated RTE,
COM / ComXf / DiagXf / Dcm generated code, ECUC + system ARXML, DBC) and
produces evidence that the following Safety Manual items are fulfilled:

    SMI          Requirement                                     Inputs per request row
    -----------  ----------------------------------------------  -------------------------------------------
    SMI-2123     All connected SWCs expect same converted data   Component(s) + RTE (API or RTE variable)
    SMI-324 CS   SWC connections as intended (client/server)     Source + API + Call function / variable
    SMI-2063     Executable entities triggered correctly         Runnable + Task
    SMI-2065     Inter-ECU S/R and C/S work as expected          Component + API
    SMI-324 NQ   SWC connections as intended (non-queued S/R)    Source + Write API, Destination + Read API
    SMI-62933    ComXf (de)serializes as expected by network     Component + API
    SMI-105506   DiagXf (de)serializes as expected by DCM        Component + API   (DID derived)
    SMI-1055     Rte_Mode provides the active mode (CREQ-1055)   Component + API

    Optional "Expected_*" columns (cycle, offset, trigger, ECU, endianness ...) can be added to any row to
    turn REVIEW verdicts into PASS/FAIL.  See the template (--template) sheet 'Columns_per_SMI'.

Results: one folder per SMI inside the chosen output folder, each holding an
Excel workbook (Summary / Checks / Evidence / Details / Gallery / Info) and
PNG evidence pictures (code snippets with highlighted lines, connection
diagrams, PDU bit layouts, summary cards).  A master workbook is written to
the output root.

PRIVACY / CONFIDENTIALITY
    100 % local.  No network access, no telemetry, no cloud services.  The
    only files written are the reports in the output folder and an index
    cache in the user's local profile (can be disabled in Settings).

USAGE
    python smi_analyzer.py                       -> GUI
    python smi_analyzer.py --selftest            -> built-in self test
    python smi_analyzer.py --template req.xlsx   -> write batch template
    python smi_analyzer.py --sandbox S --out O --excel requests.xlsx
    python smi_analyzer.py --sandbox S --out O --smi "324 not queued" \
           --src-component CtApSpeed --src-api Rte_Write_PpSpeed_DeSpeed \
           --dst-component CtApDisplay --dst-api Rte_Read_RpSpeed_DeSpeed
    python smi_analyzer.py --sandbox S --out O --smi 2063 --runnable RE_Speed_10ms --task OsTask_App_10ms

REQUIREMENTS
    Python 3.9+, openpyxl, Pillow   (lxml optional - faster ARXML parsing)

NOTE
    The tool is an evidence collector with automatic verdicts.  REVIEW means
    the tool could not decide automatically; the safety engineer has the
    final word on every item.
===============================================================================
"""
